@page "/guides/spacing"

<PageTitle>Spacing · Trailblazor</PageTitle>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Headline" As="TextElement.H1">Spacing</TbText>
<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Subtitle" class="docs-lead">
    Small <code>tb-*</code> classes add padding, margin and gap on the same spacing scale the components use, so
    one-off space in your own markup stays in step with the rest of the page.
</TbText>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Try it</TbText>
<div class="docs-example">
    <TbStack Gap="4">
        <TbStack Row Gap="3" Wrap>
            <TbSelect Label="Property" @bind-Value="_property">
                <TbOption Value="@("p")">Padding</TbOption>
                <TbOption Value="@("m")">Margin</TbOption>
            </TbSelect>
            <TbSelect Label="Side" @bind-Value="_side">
                @foreach (var side in Sides)
                {
                    <TbOption Value="side.Letter">@side.Name</TbOption>
                }
            </TbSelect>
            <TbSelect Label="Step" @bind-Value="_step">
                @foreach (var (step, _) in Scale)
                {
                    <TbOption Value="step">@step</TbOption>
                }
            </TbSelect>
        </TbStack>
        <div class="docs-spacing-frame">
            <div class="@ClassName docs-spacing-box">
                <code>@ClassName</code>
            </div>
        </div>
    </TbStack>
</div>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">The classes</TbText>
<TbText>
    Each class is a property, an optional side and a step: <code>tb-p-4</code> pads every side by step 4, and
    <code>tb-mt-2</code> adds step 2 of margin before the element. <code>tb-m-auto</code> and its sides set
    <code>auto</code> margins, and <code>tb-gap-*</code> spaces the children of your own flex and grid containers.
</TbText>
<div class="docs-api" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Spacing classes">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Classes</th>
                <th scope="col">Sets</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var (classes, sets) in Classes)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td><code>@classes</code></td>
                    <td>@sets</td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">The scale</TbText>
<TbText>
    The steps are the <code>--tb-space-*</code> tokens, so a theme that changes them changes every class too.
</TbText>
<div class="docs-api" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Spacing steps">
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th scope="col">Step</th>
                <th scope="col">Token</th>
                <th scope="col">Default</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            @foreach (var (step, size) in Scale)
            {
                <tr>
                    <td>@step</td>
                    <td><code>--tb-space-@step</code></td>
                    <td><code>@size</code></td>
                </tr>
            }
        </tbody>
    </table>
</div>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Sides follow the writing direction</TbText>
<TbText>
    The sides are logical. <code>x</code> and <code>y</code> are the inline and block axes; <code>t</code> and
    <code>b</code> are the block start and end, which are top and bottom in most languages; <code>s</code> and
    <code>e</code> are the inline start and end, so <code>tb-ms-2</code> is a left margin on an English page and a
    right margin on an Arabic or Hebrew one, with no extra classes.
</TbText>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Text alignment</TbText>
<TbText>
    <code>tb-text-start</code>, <code>tb-text-center</code> and <code>tb-text-end</code> align text within its box.
    Start and end follow the writing direction, as the sides do, so <code>tb-text-end</code> puts text on the right
    of an English page and on the left of an Arabic or Hebrew one.
</TbText>

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">With TbStack and TbGrid</TbText>
<TbText>
    For space between siblings, use the layouts' own <code>Gap</code>: <code>&lt;TbStack Gap="4"&gt;</code> and
    <code>&lt;TbGrid Gap="6"&gt;</code> take the same steps as the classes. Reach for the classes for space around a
    single element, or for gaps in containers of your own.
</TbText>
<CodeBlock Label="Layouts and classes together" Code="@Together" />

<TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title" As="TextElement.H2" class="docs-section">Which style wins</TbText>
<TbText>
    The classes sit in their own cascade layer, <code>tb.utilities</code>, after the components' layer. A class on a
    component therefore beats the component's own spacing, whatever its selectors, and your own CSS, outside any
    layer, beats both, so nothing needs <code>!important</code>.
</TbText>

@code {
    // The tokens' default values, as trailblazor.css sets them.
    private static readonly (int Step, string Size)[] Scale =
    [
        (0, "0px"), (1, "0.25rem"), (2, "0.5rem"), (3, "0.75rem"), (4, "1rem"), (5, "1.25rem"), (6, "1.5rem"),
        (8, "2rem"), (10, "2.5rem"), (12, "3rem"), (16, "4rem"),
    ];

    private static readonly (string Letter, string Name)[] Sides =
    [
        ("", "All"), ("x", "Inline (x)"), ("y", "Block (y)"), ("t", "Block start (t)"), ("b", "Block end (b)"),
        ("s", "Inline start (s)"), ("e", "Inline end (e)"),
    ];

    private static readonly (string Classes, string Sets)[] Classes =
    [
        ("tb-p-{step}", "padding"),
        ("tb-px-{step}, tb-py-{step}", "padding-inline, padding-block"),
        ("tb-pt-{step}, tb-pb-{step}", "padding-block-start, padding-block-end"),
        ("tb-ps-{step}, tb-pe-{step}", "padding-inline-start, padding-inline-end"),
        ("tb-m-{step}", "margin"),
        ("tb-mx-{step}, tb-my-{step}", "margin-inline, margin-block"),
        ("tb-mt-{step}, tb-mb-{step}", "margin-block-start, margin-block-end"),
        ("tb-ms-{step}, tb-me-{step}", "margin-inline-start, margin-inline-end"),
        ("tb-m-auto, tb-mx-auto, tb-my-auto, tb-mt-auto, tb-mb-auto, tb-ms-auto, tb-me-auto", "auto margins"),
        ("tb-gap-{step}, tb-gap-x-{step}, tb-gap-y-{step}", "gap, column-gap, row-gap"),
    ];

    private const string Together = """
        <TbStack Row Gap="4" Align="Align.Center" class="tb-p-6">
            <TbText TextStyle="TextStyle.Title">Trail report</TbText>
            <TbButton class="tb-ms-auto">Share</TbButton>
        </TbStack>
        """;

    private string _property = "p";
    private string _side = "";
    private int _step = 4;

    private string ClassName => $"tb-{_property}{_side}-{_step}";
}
